      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am on the same page regarding all renderStepID information being encapsulated in the key already. However, I\u0027m less clear on whether \"a given renderStep type + all the other variables will always have the same number of texture/samplers and uniform blocks\". I thought so as well, but it was unclear to me whether the renderStepId housed information on the NUMBER of texture/samplers and uniforms, or simply whether they had them at all (see https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp#74 ; https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/graphite/Renderer.h#161). \n\nI did observe that there exists a numUniforms() method within Renderer.h, but I don\u0027t see that being used for the purpose of renderStepID generation. RendererProvider.cpp seems to create the actual RenderStep objects, and I don\u0027t see that information being taken into account there for determining when we need to create a new render step id (which just uses next_id()). But if I\u0027m missing it, please let me know.\n\nThat being said... You may be right, because removing these components of the key seems to retain functionality for a sampling of images I\u0027ve observed (at least along with the other updates I\u0027ve made).",
